Subject-level QC (`drop_subject_outliers`, and `run_qc` with subject QC on) raises when `subject_col` is not a coordinate of the container. It used to fall back to the observation IDs or positions, so every epoch counted as its own subject: a misspelled column turned subject QC into a second epoch QC with no error. Epoch QC only counts subjects, so it still runs and reports `n_subjects_in` and `n_subjects_out` as `None` when the subjects are unknown, instead of the number of epochs.
